schema: token-twins-labels/1
corpus: benchmarks/token-twins-labels
labeled: 2026-10-15
labeling: "human judgment from reading the source, recorded before any verdict, subgroup or partial-block implementation was scored; see benchmarks/token-twins.md#labeled-corpus-for-verdicts-subgroups-and-partial-blocks"
reference_normalization: broad
analysis_flags[4]: --min-lines,5,--min-tokens,30
partial_block_minimum: "assumed equal to the analysis thresholds; every expected block spans at least 7 lines and 60 source tokens, every below-minimum negative at most 3 shared lines"
levels[4]{level,meaning}:
  REAL,"the members encode one rule; replacing them with one function needs no new parameter beyond names, or only wraps context (a decorator or attribute) around one shared body"
  SUSPICIOUS,"plausibly one rule, but consolidation needs parameters for differing members, callees, types, literals or registration context, or the group mixes families; a reviewer must decide"
  FALSE_POSITIVE,"the shape coincides but the members implement different rules or effects; merging them would couple unrelated code or change behavior"
  ambiguous,"reasonable reviewers disagree; excluded from the confusion matrix and counted separately"
partitions[3]{value,meaning}:
  single,"the whole labeled group is one family; a subgroup report must not split it"
  split,"members carry a family letter; the expected partition groups members by family"
  unscored,"no partition claim (pairs whose members are neither one family nor clearly two)"
cases[31]{id,category,language,verdict,partition,rationale}:
  py-real-rows,renaming,python,REAL,single,"consistent renaming of locals and parameters; same keys, members, callees and literals"
  py-real-methods,renaming,python,REAL,single,"same total-with-tax rule in two classes; only locals differ and both read self.lines"
  py-single-chunks,renaming,python,REAL,single,"three consistent renamings of one batching generator"
  py-calls-identical,call-only,python,REAL,single,"identical request trace calls copied into two handlers; only receiver and parameter names differ"
  py-ctx-cache,context,python,REAL,single,"identical bodies; the cached variant should wrap the plain function instead of repeating it, so the decorator difference does not justify two bodies"
  py-ctx-static,context,python,REAL,single,"a staticmethod copy of a module helper with one renamed parameter; placement does not change the rule"
  rs-real-checksum,renaming,rust,REAL,single,"consistent renaming; visibility differs, which is not structure"
  rs-real-methods,renaming,rust,REAL,single,"same total-weight rule in two containers of the same Item type; only locals differ"
  rs-single-pairs,renaming,rust,REAL,single,"three consistent renamings of one key=value parser"
  rs-calls-identical,call-only,rust,REAL,single,"identical banner macro calls in two binaries; only the parameter name differs"
  rs-ctx-inline,context,rust,REAL,single,"#[inline] is an optimization hint; the clamp rule and its data flow are identical"
  py-susp-retry,literal,python,SUSPICIOUS,unscored,"one retry-GET rule, but endpoint, attempt count, timeout and backoff differ and may be deliberate per-resource policy"
  py-susp-types,type,python,SUSPICIOUS,unscored,"one range check; bounds and annotations differ (int port versus float ratio), so a merge needs bounds parameters and a type decision"
  py-split-members,families,python,SUSPICIOUS,split,"family A sums paid amounts skipping cancelled rows, family B sums late days skipping returned loans; each family is a real copy, the whole group is not"
  py-split-dataflow,families,python,SUSPICIOUS,split,"two scale copies are one rule; skew_points multiplies y by x, a different transform with a not-one-to-one identifier pattern"
  py-ctx-routes,context,python,SUSPICIOUS,unscored,"handlers registered on different routes must stay separate; the shared pagination body could become a helper taking the model class"
  rs-susp-types,type,rust,SUSPICIOUS,unscored,"one averaging rule over u32 and u64; a generic version is plausible but overflow behavior and casts differ by width"
  rs-susp-retry,literal,rust,SUSPICIOUS,unscored,"one retry loop; target URL member, timeout, attempt limit and sleep differ and may be deliberate policy"
  rs-split-sinks,families,rust,SUSPICIOUS,split,"family A appends live records to a writer, family B feeds non-empty blocks to a hasher; each family is a real copy"
  py-fp-domains,members,python,FALSE_POSITIVE,unscored,"order discount and parcel surcharge share only a gated-product shape; members and reasons to change are unrelated"
  py-fp-effects,callees,python,FALSE_POSITIVE,unscored,"sending notifications and revoking tokens have opposite effects; callees, members and audit labels differ"
  py-fp-dataflow,dataflow,python,FALSE_POSITIVE,unscored,"squared error multiplies the deviation by itself, the cross moment by the sample; the identifier pattern is not one-to-one"
  py-calls-sinks,call-only,python,FALSE_POSITIVE,unscored,"metrics emission and audit recording call different methods with different effects; only the call shape matches"
  rs-fp-domains,members,rust,FALSE_POSITIVE,unscored,"seat booking and account withdrawal share a check-and-decrement shape over unrelated aggregates and error types"
  rs-fp-dataflow,dataflow,rust,FALSE_POSITIVE,unscored,"squared deviation versus deviation times value; the identifier pattern is not one-to-one"
  rs-calls-sinks,call-only,rust,FALSE_POSITIVE,unscored,"debug logging and gauge export are different sinks; only the macro call shape matches"
  rs-ctx-platform,context,rust,FALSE_POSITIVE,unscored,"mutually exclusive cfg alternatives: only one exists in any build, and the environment variable and path segments differ"
  py-amb-builders,api-convention,python,ambiguous,unscored,"public schema builders whose shared shape is the API convention; some reviewers merge them, others keep each builder explicit"
  py-amb-tests,tests,python,ambiguous,unscored,"tests differing only in input data; parametrizing is reasonable, keeping two readable scenarios is too"
  py-calls-fields,call-only,python,ambiguous,unscored,"same logger, different events and fields; a field-table helper is possible but of debatable value"
  rs-ctx-test-oracle,context,rust,ambiguous,unscored,"a test module re-implements the production escaper; it may be an independent oracle or a copy that should call production code"
